/// known-gap: interp does not fill in expressions in braces
/// Placeholders are worked out in the order they are written (a call that
/// changes `n` comes before a later `{n}`), and a call to a name that is
/// neither an action nor a builtin stays as written.
n | 0
act bump(x)
    n |= n + 1
    return n
xx
say("{bump(n)} {n}")
x | 1
say("template {nope(x)} stays")
say("css stays {unknown_fn()}")
say("len {:len([1,2])}")
say("{n} then {bump(n)} then {n}")
